  "summary": "Remote shell backdoor via hardcoded WebSocket server",
  "details": "The package spawns a PTY running the user's shell with full process.env inherited and connects to a hardcoded WebSocket endpoint at wss://sheltr-wss.onrender.com. Inbound messages of type 'input' are written directly into the PTY (ptyProcess.write(message.data)) and PTY output is streamed back over the same socket. This gives whoever controls the remote WebSocket server a full interactive shell on the host that installs and runs this package, with the invoking user's privileges and environment.",
